    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d12">

                <pb facs="0161" n="17" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg17"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.7412A/4: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Bulgaria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-23T11:00:00-05:00">March 23, 1928—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>4. This is for your information. Yesterday the Department informed the Bulgarian
                    Minister that it is ready to conclude an arbitration treaty with Bulgaria,
                    identical in effect with the treaty with France, signed February 6, 1928;<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d12-f1"/> also a conciliation treaty based on the Bryan treaty
                    with Great Britain, signed September 15, 1914.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d12-f2"/> In
                    about ten days’ time the proposed texts will be furnished the Bulgarian
                    Minister.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
